2️⃣ Big-O Time Complexity ⭐

1) Direct access        → O(1) 
 - students[2]

2) One loop             → O(n)
- for student in students:
    print(student)

3) Separate loops       → O(n)
- for student in students:
    print(student)

for student in students:
    print(student)

4) Nested 2 loops       → O(n²)
- for student1 in students:
    for student2 in students:
        print(student1, student2)

5) Nested 3 loops       → O(n³)
- for a in range(n):
    for b in range(n):
        for c in range(n):
            print(a, b, c)

6) Half each time       → O(log n)
- 
Efficient sorting    → O(n log n)
Some branching recursion → O(2ⁿ)
